    "2.3 Write property tests for checkpoint/rollback over a small-model session": {
      "status": "failed",
      "failingExample": "Property 1 (Rollback is exact — deterministic generate equals), Falsifiable after 2 tests and 2 shrinks:\n  prefix (std::string) = \" \"\n  extra  (std::string) = \"d\"\nAssertion: RC_ASSERT(after_rollback.content == fresh_gen.content) at tests/unit/llama_session_test.cpp:171\nExpands to: \"Suddenled, a big,\" == \"\\\"I want to go to the park\"\n\nThe position arm of Property 1 passes (position() is restored exactly to the checkpoint, and Properties 2 & 3 pass), so the KV *position* rollback is exact. What fails is the deterministic-continuation arm: a greedy generate AFTER rollback_to(checkpoint) does not match a greedy generate from a fresh session that only decoded the prefix.\n\nRoot-cause (real implementation finding, test left intact): LlamaSession::rollback_to wipes KV cells [checkpoint,end) via llama_memory_seq_rm and resets pos_, but it does NOT refresh the context's cached logits. LlamaCppBackend::generate then samples its FIRST token from llama_sampler_sample(ctx, /*idx=*/-1), i.e. the logits of the LAST decoded token — which after a rollback are the logits that followed the now-wiped `extra` tokens, not the logits following the prefix at position checkpoint-1. So the post-rollback continuation is seeded from stale logits and diverges from the fresh prefix-only continuation. generate()'s own comment assumes idx==-1 \"samples from the right position\", which is true after an append but false immediately after a rollback_to. Fix belongs in the implementation (re-establish logits at the resume position after rollback — e.g. re-decode the last pre-checkpoint token, or have generate detect a rollback and re-prime), not in the test.",
      "lastRunTimestamp": 1793836264466
    }
  },
